  abstract = {Bohannan analyzes the dispute resolution mechanisms of the Tiv of Nigeria. He highlights the distinction between applying rigid legal codes (the jural/formalist approach) and restorative community consensus. In clear-cut disputes over debt or brideprice, rules are systematically applied. However, in hard cases, Tiv judges prioritize 'repairing the tar' (the community's social fabric). The decision-making process becomes highly realist and flexible, utilizing public moots to address underlying social tensions, personal grievances, and witchcraft accusations to restore total social harmony.}
